  "description": "Codex (OpenAI) CLI/desktop telemetry \u2014 turns, tokens, latency, tools, and events. No cost panels (ChatGPT-subscription auth emits no cost telemetry). Sparse-event/occurrence panels use Loki count_over_time, not expired-counter increase(). OTL fix 2026-08-24: the Turns/Tool Calls/Threads/Codex-Events/Codex-Errors Loki panels were matching the log BODY, which is always empty for structured codex.* events (all data rides as structured metadata) \u2014 fixed to metadata pipeline filters (`| event_name=\"...\"`, `| success=\"false\"`). TTFT/Turn-Latency/TTFM panels pointed at metric names that no longer exist (`*_seconds_bucket` was renamed to `*_duration_ms_milliseconds_bucket` upstream) \u2014 fixed + unit corrected to ms. IMPORTANT: codex_exec (headless relay workers) emits NO codex_conversation_turn_count_total / codex_turn_token_usage_* / codex_turn_e2e_duration_ms_* \u2014 Tokens, Cache Hit Rate, Turn Rate by Model, Tokens by Model, and Turn Latency reflect Codex Desktop/app-server ONLY. Headless relay turns/tokens/tool-calls by ticket live in the Codex \u2014 Relay Attribution row below (Loki + the few codex_exec-native Prometheus metrics: codex_tool_call_total, codex_thread_started_total, codex_turn_ttft/ttfm_duration_ms). Codex has NO real cost telemetry (verified 2026-08-24 across the rollout JSONLs, the OTLP feed, and the OpenAI platform Costs API -- see provisioning/prometheus/codex-price-table.md); the Codex \u2014 CALCULATED Cost row prices the same headless-relay tokens at OpenAI's published API list price and is labeled CALCULATED throughout -- never treat it as a real bill.",
